From mcarlson at fhcrc.org  Wed May  7 20:23:11 2008
From: mcarlson at fhcrc.org (Marc Carlson)
Date: Wed, 07 May 2008 11:23:11 -0700
Subject: [BioC] AnnBuilder: Where to find which files are needed from
 AnnBuilder:::getSrcUrl("all", <ORGANISM>) locations?
In-Reply-To: <fvsgbk$8lg$1@ger.gmane.org>
References: <fvsgbk$8lg$1@ger.gmane.org>
Message-ID: <4821F38F.1040705@fhcrc.org>

Hi Johannes,

Since you are making packages for mouse I think you might want to use 
our newer SQLForge functions (found inside of the AnnotationDbi package) 
to make these.  Anbuilder is really being "phased out" except for those 
rare niche organisms that we have not been able to make databases for.  
There is a vignette online here for SQLForge:

http://www.bioconductor.org/packages/2.2/bioc/html/AnnotationDbi.html

SQLForge will make the newer .db style annotation packages as long as 
you are using a supported organism (and it looks like you are).  Let me 
know if you have questions about SQLForge.


    Marc



